This image illustrates the conceptual dendrimer-like structure of the alpha-D-glucan nanoparticles (Nano-11) described in the PDF. These highly branched nanoparticles, derived from phytoglycogen, are designed to have a high molecular density increasing from the center to the surface. Their dendrimer-like nature is a key characteristic enabling their functionalization and role as effective vaccine adjuvants, facilitating antigen delivery to dendritic cells and enhancing immune responses.